From 03aa5816199b5a95da37dad6605b6b136bfdcda7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Assistant <assistant@local>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 04:14:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add hashtags to Facebook, LinkedIn, Telegram, Pinterest
 (Instagram/TikTok already had them)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Instagram and TikTok generators already produced a structured hashtags[]
array in metadata and their publishers appended it to the outgoing
caption. Facebook, LinkedIn, Telegram, and Pinterest had neither — their
generators never asked the model for hashtags, and their publishers just
sent contentAsset.body as-is with nothing appended.

Added a shared buildCaptionWithHashtags() helper in lib/publishers/base.js
(the same join logic Instagram's publisher already had inline, pulled out
so every publisher uses one implementation instead of four copies), then:

- facebook.js / linkedin.js / telegram.js / pinterest.js generators: added
  a hashtags field to each prompt (tuned per-platform — Facebook/LinkedIn
  keep it to 3-5 broad/professional tags rather than IG-style 15-20 tag
  spam; Pinterest/Telegram get a handful of subject/exam tags), and store
  the result in metadata.hashtags alongside the existing slides/image_brief.
- facebook.js / linkedin.js / telegram.js / pinterest.js publishers: use
  buildCaptionWithHashtags(contentAsset.body, contentAsset.metadata?.hashtags)
  instead of sending contentAsset.body / contentAsset.title description
  unchanged, so the generated hashtags now actually reach the post.
